{"conversation_id":"e4fbf30d-58bb-4263-9981-af6c3994b3fb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Reviewed `git diff f954d5ec..HEAD` (`cbb166e4`) and appended the r3 confirmation section to [1795257159499-reviewer-p1prime-yrt-effect-int-unified-clj.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/collab/yang-clojure/1795257159499-reviewer-p1prime-yrt-effect-int-unified-clj.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md):\n\n1. **Bundled lexical scope ([prelude.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc#L205-L219), [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2050-L2055)):**\n   - **§7.4 bundled door enforcement:** `prelude/uast` ([prelude.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc#L194-L202)) is unchanged; `:clj/bundled-runtime` stays inside `prelude/uast`'s closed 0-arg lambda while `body` (`helpers`) is sequenced as a sibling after `uast` and `(clj/init!)`. Neither `mark-bundled-calls` (`:walker`) nor `bundle-graph` (`:semantic`, `:stack`, `:register`) grants provenance-door authority to `body`.\n   - **§4.3 capture-safety \u0026 portability:** The outer scope binds only reserved `[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__add dsg__lte]` to portable guest closures (`bundled-primitive-forms`), while bare `[get = assoc + \u003c=]` stay scoped to `shared` and `uast` so guest definitions can still shadow bare primitive names without affecting runtime frames.\n\n2. **Intra-unit direct-call fast path ([clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1111-L1149), [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1354-L1362), [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2014-L2058)):**\n   - `dsg__make_local` still constructs and returns a genuine cell-backed callable via `clj/make-callable`.\n   - `dsg__invoke_local` verifies both `(data/content= (data/nth registered 0) callee)` and `(data/content= (data/nth registered 1) (cell/get callee))` before calling `local-entry`, falling back to `dsg__invoke_dynamic` → `clj/invoke-callable` on redefinition or cell mutation (covered by [effect_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/rt/effect_test.cljc#L196-L197)).\n   - All tuple reads use `data/nth`, map accesses use `clj/prim-get`/`clj/prim-assoc`, and all helper bindings are lexical to the unit so linked mode (`lower-unit`) adds zero free names.\n\nVERDICT: CONFIRMED-CLOSED\nCONFIRMED-CLOSED\n","duration_seconds":9074.845163,"num_turns":3,"usage":{"input_tokens":557545,"output_tokens":44719,"thinking_tokens":32329,"cache_read_tokens":5491021,"total_tokens":602264}}
